ooks that way  you can't wake a person who is  pretending to be asleep  it is less of a problem to be poor than  to be dishonest  one finger cannot lift a pebble  Beware of the man who does not talk and  the dog that does not bark  all dreams spin out from the same web  old age is not as honorable as death but  most people want it  even a small Mouse has anger  if a man is as wise as a serpent he can  afford to be as harmless as a dove  the rainbow is a sign from him who is in  all things  walked lightly in the spring Mother  Earth is pregnant  when a man moves away from nature his  heart becomes hard  everything that power does it does in a  circle  a brave man dies but once a coward many  times  a man or woman with many children has  many homes  seek wisdom not knowledge knowledge is  of the past wisdom is of the future  if you see no reason for giving thanks  the fault lies in yourself  a good Chief gives he does not take  coyote is always out there waiting and  coyote is always hungry  listening to a liar is like drinking  warm water  every animal knows more than you do  to touch the Earth is to have harmony  with nature  when a fox walks lame the old rabbit  jumps  many have fallen with a bottle in their  hand  a starving man will eat with the wolf  a danger foreseen is half avoided  the coward shoots with eyes shut  is easy to be to be brave from a  distance  the bird who has eaten cannot fly with  the bird who is hungry  ask questions from your heart and you  will be answered from your heart  a hungry stomach makes a short prayer  do not wrong or hate your neighbor for  it is not he that you wrong but yourself  make my enemy brave and strong so that  if defeated I will not be ashamed  cherish youth but trust old age  sharing and giving are the ways of God  we are all one child spinning through  mother sky  person is his own judge  we are made from Mother Earth and we go  back to Mother Earth  it is no longer good enough to cry peace  we must act peace live peace and live in  peace  there are many good moccasin tracks  along the trail of a Straight Arrow  a rocky Vineyard does not need a prayer  but a pickaxe  with all things and in all things we are  relatives  the one who tells the stories rules the  world  the Frog does not drink up the pond in  which he lives  a people without a history is like the  wind over buffalo grass  the Moon is not shamed by The Barking of  dogs  white men have too many chiefs  if a man is to do something more than  human he must have more than human  powers  the soul would have no rainbow if the  eye had no tears  wisdom comes only when you stop looking  for it and start living the life the  Creator intended for you  not every sweet root gives birth to  sweet grass  take only what you need and leave the  land as you found it  it takes a thousand voices to tell a  single story  don't let yesterday use up too much of  today  no River can return to its source yet  all Rivers must have a beginning  listen or your tongue will make you deaf  man has responsibility not power  the rain falls on the just and the  unjust  each bird loves to hear himself sing  the way of the Troublemaker is thorny  God gives to each a song  a man who looks first to a woman's outer  beauty will never know her beauty Divine  for there is dust upon his eyes and he  is blind  a man must make his own arrows  after dark all cats are leopards  when you die you will be spoken of as  those in the sky like the stars

